        "date_dead_since": null,
        "date_published": "2026-11-19T16:34:04+00:00",
        "description": "<p>Hey HN, I'm Daniel, founder of Onlook (<a href=\"https://github.com/onlook-dev/onlook\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://github.com/onlook-dev/onlook</a> and onlook.com).<p>Onlook is a desktop app that puts a canvas on top of your real codebase, letting you design directly in code with the agent you already use. Over 25,000 designers and developers have supported the project, 100+ have contributed, and it's been the #1 trending repo in the world twice. We just rebuilt the entire product as an agentic design tool, and open-sourced it to the community.<p>Here\u2019s a demo video: (<a href=\"https://youtu.be/BogcYWf4siM\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://youtu.be/BogcYWf4siM</a>)<p>If you're an engineer, traditional engineering tools are largely built for convergence, whereas designers tend to explore and diverge on ideas. Onlook gives designers a familiar canvas while managing all of the dev processes that get between them and making mind-blowing designs in code. Designers can work on a multiple simultaneous wor",
