        "description": "<p>I wanted to build a full weight-space programming loop entirely in the browser with WebGPU: let an LLM inspect Qwen3.5-0.8B, edit its weights, evaluate, and repeat.<p>the full loop needed too much VRAM. so I turned it into an interactive walkthrough of a concrete example: editing 0.016% of a model's weights to reduce reasoning loops, no gradient descent.<p>Based on exp8 of \u201cSparks of Weight-Space Programming.\u201d: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50341174\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50341174</a></p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50561436\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50561436</a></p>\n<p>Points: 3</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>",
